            <h1 class="h2" id="cookies-title">Cookie Notice</h1>
            <div class="legal__meta"><span>Başak Feyzioğlu (Libre Studio)</span><span>Last updated 15 October 2026</span></div>
          </header>

          <section id="controller">
            <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
            <p>This notice informs visitors of librestudio.co under Article 10 of the Turkish Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 (“KVKK”). The data controller is Başak Feyzioğlu (“Libre Studio”).</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Tax ID (VKN): 3850912842</li>
              <li>Business Address: Sinanoba Mah. Aktan Sok. No:58T Büyükçekmece / Istanbul / Turkiye</li>
              <li>E-mail: <a href="mailto:{{email}}">{{email}}</a> · Phone: <a href="tel:+905377950969">+90 537 795 0969</a></li>
            </ul>
            <p>This notice covers visiting the website and cookies only. For applicants, the <a href="/privacy/">Candidate &amp; Freelancer Privacy Notice</a> applies.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="summary">
            <h2>2. In Short</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>librestudio.co sets no cookies unless you accept analytics. With your consent, Google Analytics 4 measures how the site is used. If you decline or make no choice, Google Analytics is not loaded and no request is sent to Google.</li>
              <li>The site loads no advertising tools and no third-party content (embedded forms, videos or fonts).</li>
              <li>You can change your choice at any time with the “Cookie settings” link in the footer of every page.</li>
              <li>Our application form is not shown on this site. The button on the application page opens it on ClickUp's own site (forms.clickup.com) in a new tab. ClickUp decides which cookies are set there.</li>
              <li>If you would rather not use ClickUp, you can apply by email. That choice does not affect how your application is assessed.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="site">
            <h2>3. This Site's Cookies and Storage</h2>
            <p>On your first visit, a banner asks whether you accept analytics, with “Accept” and “Decline” buttons. Until you press “Accept”, the site does not load Google Analytics, sends no request to Google and writes no cookies.</p>
            <p>Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage (localStorage) under the key <code>ls-consent</code>, with the value “granted” or “denied”. This entry is strictly necessary to remember your choice. It holds no personal data, is not a cookie and is never sent to us or to anyone else.</p>
            <p>If you accept, Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC, USA) sets the two cookies listed in section 5 on .librestudio.co. We use them for statistics: which pages are visited, how visitors arrive (search, links), the device used and approximate location (country and city, derived by Google). This helps us improve the site. Our Google Analytics settings:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Google signals are off. No advertising features and no ads personalisation are used.</li>
              <li>Data is kept for 2 months.</li>
              <li>Google states that Google Analytics 4 does not log or store IP addresses.</li>
              <li>Consent Mode v2: advertising storage, ad user data and ad personalisation are always denied. Analytics storage is granted only after you accept.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Fonts and the showreel are served from this site, not from third parties.</p>
            <p>The site is hosted by Netlify, Inc. (USA). To deliver the site and protect it from abuse, Netlify processes technical data such as IP address, browser details and the page requested in its server logs on every visit. This uses no cookies and relies on the controller's legitimate interest (KVKK Art. 5/2-f).</p>
          </section>

          <section id="clickup">
            <h2>4. The Application Form (ClickUp)</h2>
            <p>Our application form is hosted by ClickUp (Mango Technologies, Inc., USA). When you press the button on the <a href="/careers/apply/">application page</a>, the form opens on ClickUp's own site. There, ClickUp and the services it works with (Google, PartnerStack, Segment, Datadog) may set cookies and use browser storage on your device; some are for analytics and advertising. ClickUp decides and manages these cookies under its own policies; this site does not load them.</p>
            <p>The application page gives you two options:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Open the form:</strong> it opens on ClickUp's site, where the cookies below may be set.</li>
              <li><strong>Email:</strong> send your portfolio link to <a href="mailto:{{email}}">{{email}}</a>; no ClickUp cookies are set.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="list">
